message.content:
This appears to be based on a CBP ruling about vibration platforms. Electric massagers are classified under 8543.70 or 9019.10. Heading 9019 covers "Mechano-therapy appliances; massage apparatus," and subheading 9019.10 covers these appliances. 9019.10.20 covers "Electro-mechanical massage apparatus" or similar, and 9019.10.2090 is "Other" for massage apparatus.

The HTS structure is: 9019.10.10 "Electrically operated" (with 9019.10.10 as the statistical suffix), 9019.10.20 "Other: Massage apparatus", and 9019.10.90 "Other". The more exact structure is 9019.10.20 "Massage apparatus... Electrically operated" with 9019.10.2010 and 9019.10.2090. The CBP ruling for vibration foot massagers likely used 9019.10.2090, since a platform vibration machine was found not to be exercise equipment (9506.91). I'll go with 9019.10.2090.

{"hts_code": "9019.10.2090", "reason": "The device is an electrically operated therapeutic vibration massage apparatus for seated or reclined use, not exercise equipment, so it falls under heading 9019 as massage apparatus (9019.10.20) rather than heading 9506."}
